# IA Mentoring Evidence

## Interaction 1: Normalization and Data Integrity
**Date:** March 2026  
**Participants:** Full Cell Team  

### Prompt Description
[span_4](start_span)We asked our **Senior DBA Mentor** to explain the theoretical foundations of the three Normal Forms (1NF, 2NF, 3NF) and how to avoid orphan data[span_4](end_span).

### Screenshot
![AI Normalization Guidance](./ai_mentoring_normalization.jpg)

### Learning Outcomes
* **[span_5](start_span)Guidance:** The IA provided generic examples instead of solving our specific flight agency project, forcing us to apply the logic ourselves[span_5](end_span).
* **[span_6](start_span)1NF Knowledge:** We learned that every column must contain atomic values and no repeating groups are allowed[span_6](end_span).
* **[span_7](start_span)Integrity:** We understood that orphan data is avoided through the correct implementation of Foreign Keys (FK) and constraints[span_7](end_span).
